1|//! Equivalence-Based Approval Hashing (Task 7C.2.2)
2|//!
3|//! SHA-256 hash of `[actor_id, bot_id, tool_ref, effect, scope, stable(target), stable(args)]`
4|//! enables retry of the same action to reuse an existing approval instead of re-prompting.
5|//!
6|//! Four-tier decision source: safety > team_rule > personal_rule > auto_review > default.
7|//! Safety tier always wins and cannot be overridden.
8|//!
9|//! Distinct refusal messages for each denial reason.
10|//! Continuation capture via tokio task-local (AsyncLocalStorage equivalent).
11|//! Escalation as an ungated tool — always available as a safe exit.
12|//!
13|//! Source: OpenDuet `approvals/service.ts`, `escalation.ts`
14|
15|use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};
16|use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
17|use sha2::{Digest, Sha256};
18|use std::collections::HashMap;
19|use std::sync::Mutex;
